1.9) lights the sides in shadow. Karma values to restore for Karma: dome 1.0 / 0, key 1.5.\n- 6 October 2026 : WHERE the Cycles settings are. There is NO Cycles node in Solaris (searched all node types for \"cycles\"): the delegate is configured by attributes on the render settings prim, `cycles:samples`, `cycles:device`, `cycles:threads`, `cycles:time_limit`, `cycles:integrator:*` (max_bounce and others, `use_denoise`, `use_adaptive_sampling`, `use_light_tree`); the viewport quality is also set from the viewport's own render options (the small pencil icon next to the \"Cycles Persp\" label). To author them in the graph: an Edit Properties or Python LOP that sets the attribute on `/Render/rendersettings`. Not done yet: the display flag must stay BEFORE `lt_karma`, so such a node would have to sit before it.\n- 6 October 2026 : what is still different from Karma: Cycles has no Karma Principled features (no sheen, no translucency from the Principled), the petals are paler, the lighting is plain. A custom Cycles material (MaterialX or Cycles shader network) would be the next step for a real match.\n\n## 6 October 2026 : Cycles lookdev is now driven by an editable file\n\n- 6 October 2026 (Matthieu: \"tenir dans le skill une section à jour avec les paramètres que je peux éditer\"): `CyclesLookdev1.md` next to this file holds a JSON block (dome, key, fill, normal map on or off, viewport delegate, display node) with a table that explains each value. Matthieu edits it, says \"applique le lookdev Cycles\", and the agent runs `Scripts/ApplyCyclesLookdev.py` in the live Houdini (`exec(open(path).read())` through `houdini_hom` live), which writes the values to `lt_dome`, `lt_key`, `lt_fill` and `lt_cycles_preview_fix`, sets the Cycles delegate, saves the hip, then the viewport is captured with `CaptureHoudiniViewport.sh` to check it.\n- 6 October 2026 : FINDING: the Cycles delegate IGNORES the `scale` and `bias` of the preview normal texture (the viewport capture was identical